// PARAM: --analysis interval
// No verdict annotations: a parse-rejection case. A local shares its
// procedure's scope with that procedure's formals, so a local may not
// repeat one of them -- the name would carry two declarations, at two
// kinds, in one scope.
int32 f(int32 n) {
  int32 n;
  return n
}
void main() {
  f(1)
}
